Now that you've ascended a melee-class, I suggest you do some cross-
class training and take one of the other types:

Ranged class:  Ranger, Rogue

These classes depend heavily on throwing or shooting weapons.  Being
able to ascend one of these will definitely help prepare you for

Magic-using classes:
Wizard, Archaeologist, Knight

Once you can do that, you are now ready for:

The jack-of-all-trades class: The Tourist.

The tourist starts off very weak, but they have skill slots in just
about everything, allowing them to be customized for playing style.
If you can
overcome the wizard's initial strength penalty and fight with ranged
weapons like a rogue, IMO you can ascend a tourist.

Hard classes: Priest, Monk.

I say these are 'hard' because they have few skill slots available for
ranged weapons, don't start with much useful magic, and are mediocre
at melee.
They have lots of weaknesses and very few strengths. Moreover, monk is
crippled by an inability to wear body armor until very high-level,
meaning that early protection is pretty much a must.  But if you can
ascend multiple other classes, you just might have the skill set
needed to ascend this one.  Caveman can be a trainer for these
classes, because it's a semi-melee class that starts with  a miserable
weapon.

